import{_ as t,o as a,c as s,a5 as n}from"./chunks/framework.CsGesDJn.js";const p=JSON.parse('{"title":"DA-1013 verification — 2026-09-24","description":"","frontmatter":{},"headers":[],"relativePath":"feature/admin-management/system-health/evidence.md","filePath":"feature/admin-management/system-health/evidence.md"}'),i={name:"feature/admin-management/system-health/evidence.md"};function r(o,e,d,c,l,u){return a(),s("div",null,[...e[0]||(e[0]=[n('<h1 id="da-1013-verification-—-2026-09-24" tabindex="-1">DA-1013 verification — 2026-09-24 <a class="header-anchor" href="#da-1013-verification-—-2026-09-24" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;DA-1013 verification — 2026-09-24&quot;">​</a></h1><p>Implementation is present in Business, Gateway, Web and Infrastructure. No production deployment, host registration or application database migration was executed by these checks.</p><h2 id="checks-executed" tabindex="-1">Checks executed <a class="header-anchor" href="#checks-executed" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Checks executed&quot;">​</a></h2><table tabindex="0"><thead><tr><th>Check</th><th>Result</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Monitoring migration on isolated PostgreSQL 17</td><td>Applied successfully; real JPA ingestion/read tests use these tables</td></tr><tr><td>Business <code>mvn -q -Dtest=MonitoringApiTest,MonitoringDatabaseTest test</code> with <code>MONITORING_TEST_JDBC=jdbc:postgresql://127.0.0.1:55439/monitor_test</code></td><td>6 passed; controlled 60/90-second boundaries, duplicate/order handling, invalid/auth evidence and current ADMIN checks</td></tr><tr><td>Gateway <code>mvn -q -Dtest=MonitoringRouteTest test</code></td><td>2 passed; exact machine POST routes preserve tokens; GET requires JWT</td></tr><tr><td>Worker <code>MONITORING_DATABASE_SMOKE=true npm test</code></td><td>11 passed; HTTP/runtime/resource fixtures, four real authenticated database adapters, Redis command denial, independent heartbeat and scheduler concurrency/no-overlap</td></tr><tr><td>Web <code>npm run build</code></td><td>Passed TypeScript and production build; existing large-chunk/Vite configuration warnings</td></tr><tr><td>Web <code>npx eslint src/pages/admin/system-health</code></td><td>Passed</td></tr><tr><td>Web Playwright system-health spec</td><td>7 passed; revoked access clears both sources, 503 retains previous snapshot, filters/details, vi light/dark at 375/768/1440</td></tr><tr><td>Web full Playwright suite</td><td>51 passed, 1 failed: existing login test expects GitHub button</td></tr><tr><td>Business full Maven suite</td><td>155 reported, 1 failure, 26 errors, 1 skipped (opt-in DB test disabled in default full run)</td></tr><tr><td>Gateway full Maven suite</td><td>36 tests, 1 failure: LoggingGlobalFilterTest.orderIsLowestPrecedenceMinus1</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Redis query-denial regression was reproduced RED with a real isolated ACL user denied PING, then GREEN after classifying Redis ErrorReply as QUERY_FAILED while preserving authentication errors as UNKNOWN. The ACL user is removed by test cleanup.</p><h2 id="baseline-comparisons" tabindex="-1">Baseline comparisons <a class="header-anchor" href="#baseline-comparisons" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Baseline comparisons&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Unmodified HEAD archives were extracted under <code>tuan-research/.scratch/da1013-baseline</code>, outside application repositories. Business baseline 7470469 reproduces the same 27 failing/error test names: existing MVC tests lack JwtUtil configuration, and AuthServiceTest assertions/mocks mismatch the registration flow. Gateway baseline acd76c2 reproduces the logging-order failure in an isolated targeted run. Its archive full run also has environment-dependent application-context errors, so that full count is not treated as equivalent. Web baseline 92d3016 reproduces the same login GitHub-button failure. These unrelated sources/tests were left unchanged.</p><p>Full logs remain in each Java repository&#39;s ignored target/da1013-tests.log, the frontend ignored playwright-da1013.log, and the scratch baseline directories. Feature screenshots are generated by Playwright in ignored test-results. These are local execution artifacts, not proof of deployed behavior.</p><h2 id="test-isolation-and-safety" tabindex="-1">Test isolation and safety <a class="header-anchor" href="#test-isolation-and-safety" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Test isolation and safety&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Dedicated Docker test instances: <code>brandhub-monitoring-test-da1013</code> (PostgreSQL, localhost 55439), <code>brandhub-monitoring-redis-da1013</code> (56389), <code>brandhub-monitoring-mongo-da1013</code> (57019), <code>brandhub-monitoring-neo4j-da1013</code> (57689). Only test credentials are used. Existing <code>brandhub-postgres</code>, Redis, RabbitMQ and pgAdmin containers are not changed. The opt-in MonitoringDatabaseTest truncates its monitoring tables and must only target a disposable database.</p><h2 id="remaining-acceptance-—-do-not-mark-issues-06-07-09-complete" tabindex="-1">Remaining acceptance — do not mark issues 06/07/09 complete <a class="header-anchor" href="#remaining-acceptance-—-do-not-mark-issues-06-07-09-complete" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Remaining acceptance — do not mark issues 06/07/09 complete&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li>Supply the real host/environment/instance inventory and operator-managed secret files; select a read-only business GET route and frontend assertion.</li><li>Verify contracts for Gateway, Business, Publisher, AI, RabbitMQ and Chroma against the chosen running stack. Source-code endpoint evidence in the separate <code>brandhub-monitoring</code> repository&#39;s <code>README.md</code> is not runtime certification.</li><li>Run actual host metrics and SERVICE/CONTAINER/DATABASE/ENDPOINT probes through Gateway/Business into the ADMIN page, including UI-closed operation, worker restart, collector loss and monitoring storage failure.</li><li>Validate host replacement/redeployment identity, per-instance routing, deployed Linux metrics and runtime-proxy restrictions in that environment.</li></ul><p>HTTP and Docker fixture tests, DB adapter smoke, standalone API tests and mocked UI tests cover separate seams. They do not constitute an end-to-end deployed pipeline. The read API still depends on Gateway/Business/PostgreSQL availability; it is not independent outage monitoring.</p><p>Standards and spec reviews ran separately. Confirmed code findings were addressed: safe request-ID error logging, machine-route auth documentation, named freshness constants, HTTP evidence consistency, PostgreSQL TLS verification, Mongo SRV configuration, database query-failure classification and Redis ErrorReply handling.</p>',14)])])}const m=t(i,[["render",r]]);export{p as __pageData,m as default};
